.TH DUI 8 2026-10-25 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
dui \- download and install or update DarqOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dui
(DarqOS Updater/Installer) fetches a DarqOS distribution tarball and
runs the
.BR install (8)
script it contains.
It is used both for the first install on a host and for later
updates.
It must be run as root.
.PP
.B dui
performs these steps, stopping with an error if any fails:
.IP 1. 4
Create the
.B $DARQ_USER
account, if it doesn't exist.
.IP 2.
Create
.BR $DARQ ,
if it doesn't exist.
.IP 3.
Remove any existing
.BR $DIST ,
and create it again, empty, owned by
.BR $DARQ_USER .
.IP 4.
Download
.B $DIST_BASE/$DIST_FILE
into
.I /tmp
with
.BR wget (1).
.IP 5.
Unpack the tarball into
.BR $DIST ,
and give
.B $DARQ_USER
ownership of everything under
.BR $DARQ .
.IP 6.
Run
.BR $DIST/darq/bin/install .
.SH OPTIONS
None.
Settings are taken from the environment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARQ
Installation root.
Default:
.IR /darq .
.TP
.B DIST
Staging directory for the unpacked distribution.
Default:
.BR $DARQ/dist .
.TP
.B DIST_FILE
Name of the tarball to download.
Default:
.IR darqos-latest.tar.gz .
.TP
.B DIST_BASE
URL of the directory to download it from.
Default:
.IR https://www.0x1.org/d/darq .
.TP
.B DARQ_USER
Account that owns the installed files.
Default:
.IR darq .
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /tmp/ DIST_FILE
The downloaded tarball.
It is not removed afterwards.
.TP
.I $DIST/darq/bin/install
The install script run in the last step.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the install script completed; 1 if an earlier step failed.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is written to standard output as lines starting
.RB \(lq Ok: \(rq,
and errors to standard error as lines starting
.RB \(lq Error: \(rq.
.SH BUGS
Any existing
.B $DIST
is deleted before the download is attempted.
.PP
The check for an existing
.B $DARQ_USER
account is malformed, so the account is never created; if it were, it
would be named
.B darq
whatever
.B DARQ_USER
is set to.
.PP
The exit status of the install script is not checked.
.PP
Only tarballs built with the current
.B mkdist
can be installed: older ones keep the install script under
.IR darq/sys .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install (8),
.BR wget (1)
